comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T01:09:05.727Z","harness:codex","Production evidence 2026-07-27: Auto Release run 30228336167 passed its full gate set, created immutable tag v2026.7.27, and correctly waited for exact Release run 30228668491. That release passed coverage/static/compatibility/Sentry/package gates but failed before publication: anonymous lookup of the new target version returned absent, then the workflow attempted package-level npm access recovery even though anonymous npm view @unbrained/pm-cli resolves public 2026.7.26. NPM_TOKEN returned E403 for the unnecessary account-level access mutation. No replacement tag is permitted; fix the canonical publish guard and rerun the exact existing tag."
  "2026-07-27T01:24:54.733Z","harness:codex","Verification note: the first linked full-coverage execution failed because pm test schema mode injected an empty outer PM_PATH and the nested repository-governance coverage fixtures classified the checkout as entirely unowned. Focused tests and quality:static passed in the same run. The coverage command now clears only the outer PM_PATH/PM_GLOBAL_PATH so scripts/run-tests.mjs creates its own isolated roots; no real tracker data is exposed to tests."
  "2026-07-27T01:28:56.327Z","harness:codex","Verification follow-up: clearing the outer PM roots alone was insufficient because linked-test execution also exports PM_SOURCE_WORKSPACE_ROOT, which intentionally makes validation scan the real checkout while using the outer empty schema tracker. The final linked coverage command clears all three outer routing variables; scripts/run-tests.mjs still creates fresh isolated PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH for every test run."
  "2026-07-27T01:35:32.668Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: one NPM_PACKAGE workflow variable now supplies the anonymous target guard, public-package existence probe, access recovery, npm publish messaging, and the npm/npx/bunx verifier. A public package with a missing target version publishes without npm access mutation; exact visible versions skip; hidden packages retain fail-closed access recovery and anonymous rechecks. Executable workflow tests prove the publish, skip, and E403 refusal branches with a temporary fake npm executable. The unclaimed typo scope is absent from .github/workflows, scripts, and src and a production-tree gate rejects recurrence. Focused suite: 180 passed. Full sandboxed coverage: 376 files, 6,440 tests; statements 44,402/44,402, branches 31,517/31,517, functions 9,082/9,082, lines 43,139/43,139. ESLint, jscpd zero clones, static/docstring 100%, package boundary, token budget, SDK surface/import cost/transport floor, typecheck, and secret scan all passed. GH-746 is closed with canonical pm-2z9263 link and correct-package evidence."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T01:16:10.479Z","harness:codex","Supply-chain disposition: the unclaimed @unbraind scope is not treated as a supported compatibility alias and is removed from every production workflow, script, and source file. A repository gate rejects its reintroduction. Reserving an external npm scope requires organization-level authority outside this repository; with zero trusted references or install guidance remaining, this item records the residual namespace registration risk as accepted rather than creating or authenticating an external identity."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-27T01:35:33.379Z","harness:codex","For immutable npm releases, target-version absence and package absence are different states. Probe the exact anonymous version first, then the anonymous package identity; a public package with a missing target should publish directly, while package-access mutation belongs only in the hidden-package recovery path."
